-- Passage rg6-text-structure-p06
insert into public.passages (id, code, skill_id, sat_alignment, grade_band, title, body, status)
values ('83d1e273-ce1f-5d65-88fc-00527f9b671a', 'rg6-text-structure-p06', (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g6-text-structure'), null,
        '6-8', $q$Every Student Should Learn to Swim$q$, $q$Our town has three lakes, a river, and two public pools, yet many students at Cedar Hill Middle School cannot swim. I believe our school should offer free swimming lessons to every sixth grader. Learning to swim keeps students safe, keeps them healthy, and opens the door to new activities.

The most important reason is safety. Water is part of everyday life here, from summer trips to the lake to fishing on the river. A student who can float, tread water, and swim to the edge is far more prepared if something unexpected happens near water.

Swimming is also excellent exercise. It works the arms, legs, and heart all at once, and it is gentle on the joints. Students who do not enjoy team sports may find that swimming is an activity they truly like.

Finally, swimming leads to other opportunities. Students who can swim can join the swim team, try kayaking, or someday work as lifeguards at the town pool during summer break.

Some people argue that lessons would cost too much. However, the town pool sits empty most weekday mornings, and its manager, Ms. Delgado, has offered to share her swim instructors. The school would only need to pay for the bus ride.

Swimming is a skill that lasts a lifetime. Let's make sure every student at Cedar Hill has the chance to learn it.$q$, 'draft')
